From ff891513a9fa7b246f27e7732a8ac02b1359b363 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Willie Abrams <willie@pobox.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:06:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] kk: Add a passthrough GS for transform feedback

Use poly's passthrough GS to capture outputs when the application has no
GS. hk picks one at draw time; kk adds it during shader compilation,
before building the Metal pipelines.

The topology is dynamic within its class, so the generated GS takes the
class's points, lines or triangles, and a pipeline of the line or
triangle class gets a second variant taking the class's adjacency
primitive, as hk keys its passthrough on adjacency. The draw picks the
variant from its topology, so adjacency draws need no unroll. poly's
rasterization VS reads the input vertices and captures them, so a
variant has its own rasterization VS and Metal render pipeline; the
compute pass, count and pre-GS programs are shared.

Keep the previous stage's output types for the Metal vertex/fragment
interface.

Assisted-by: LLM
